<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive launcher icon, API 26+.

  This file stays shared; everything it references is per FLAVOUR. Both apps
  are a struck coin on graphite, and the wallet adds a base plate with WALLET
  cut out of it. They are told apart by silhouette rather than by colour, so
  the distinction survives greyscale, a 48dp launcher slot, and a colour-blind
  user.

  `monochrome` is not decoration. Android 13+ themed icons tint a single layer
  and discard colour entirely, so an app that omits this gets a filled blob.
  Reusing the foreground works here only because its shapes are CUT rather than
  overpainted: the star is a genuine hole in the face and the lettering is a
  genuine hole in the base, both via evenOdd. Paint them instead of cutting
  them and the themed icon silently degrades to a disc.

  API 24-25 predate adaptive icons and fall back to mipmap/ic_launcher.xml,
  which is per-flavour and NOT optional at minSdk 24.

  The drawables are GENERATED. Regenerate with scratchpad/make_icons.ps1, which
  emits the Android XML, the website SVG, every PNG and the Windows .ico from
  one set of constants. Hand-editing one of them desyncs the platforms.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
